"Scroll Compressor Heat Pump — Data Consistency Verification

A scroll compressor manufacturer provides the following performance data:
  - Evaporation temperature: 0 C, inlet superheat: 5 K
  - Condensation temperature: 50 C, subcooling: 4 K
  - Heating capacity: 6.30 kW
  - Electrical power input: 1.81 kW
  - Refrigerating capacity: 4.60 kW
  - Mass flow rate: 30.9 g/s, swept volume flow rate: 5.92 m3/h
  - Refrigerant: R407C

Verify that these data are consistent and calculate the overall isentropic efficiency.
"

T_ev=0
T_cd=50
Q_dot_cd=6.3E3
Q_dot_ev=4.6E3
W_dot_el=1.81E3
{COP=3.48}
COP=Q_dot_cd/W_dot_el "COP matches manufacturer's announced value"
DELTA_T_oh=5
DELTA_T_sc=4
{M_dot=30.9E-3} "optionally recompute predicted mass flow rate and swept volume V_dot_m3h"
{V_dot_m3h=5.92}

"compressor inlet:"

T_1=T_ev+DELTA_T_oh
P_1=PRESSURE(R407C,T=T_ev,x=1)
s_1=entropy(R407C,P=P_1,T=T_1)
rho_1=density(R407C,P=P_1,T=T_1)

"condenser inlet = compressor outlet"

P_2=PRESSURE(R407C,T=T_cd,x=1)
Q_dot_cd=M_dot*(h_2-h_3)
T_2=temperature(R407C,P=P_2,h=h_2)
h_2_s=enthalpy(R407C,P=P_2,s=s_1)
h_3=enthalpy(R407C,P=P_3,T=T_3)

epsilon_s_cp=(h_2_s-h_1)/(h_2-h_1)
W_dot=M_dot*(h_2-h_1)
W_dot_s=M_dot*(h_2_s-h_1)
eta_el=W_dot/W_dot_el
epsilon_s_cp_glob=W_dot_s/W_dot_el

"condenser outlet"

T_3=T_cd-DELTA_T_sc
P_3=PRESSURE(R407C,T=T_cd,x=0)

"evaporator inlet"

h_4=h_3
h_1=enthalpy(R407C,P=P_1,T=T_1)
h_4=PRESSURE(R407C,T=T_ev,p=p_4)
Q_dot_ev{_bis}=M_dot*(h_1-h_4)

"displacement volume calculation"

M_dot=V_dot*rho_1 "[kg/s]" "volumetric machine: at given speed, always draws the same volumetric flow V_dot"
V_dot_m3h=3600*V_dot "[m3/h]"

P[1]=P_1
h[1]=h_1

P[2]=P_2
h[2]=h_2

P[3]=P_3
h[3]=h_3

P[4]=P_4
h[4]=h_4

"computed mass flow and swept volume are close to manufacturer's announced values"